     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Friday, November 4, 2016 at 4:52:09 AM UTC+13, Annie wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi All,<br>I&#39;m running into issues using raster data for my habitat mask. Specifically, I have floating point GRID data file (reads as formal class raster layer in R) that I want to add as a covariate to my habitat mask. Based on secr documentation, &quot;The procedure depends on the data source spatialdata, which may be either a spatial coverage (raster or polygon) or an object with covariate values at points (another mask or traps<br>object).&quot; So raster data should be OK. These data load just fine into R but an error occurs when I try to addCovariate to the mask. <br><br><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">ndvi_14&lt;-raster(&quot;ndvi14_83cs&quot;)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">rubmask2013male &lt;- addCovariates(rubmask2014male,ndvi_14,&quot;VALUE&quot;)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in addCovariates(rubmask2014male, ndvi_14, &quot;VALUE&quot;) : \r\n  spatialdata type unrecognised or unsupported</span></pre><br>As a last resort, I can convert the raster to polygon but was wondering if anyone had a solution here. I converted my raster data from floating point to integer and secr still doesn&#39;t like recognize or support this data type. <br><br>Thanks for any comments/suggestions!<br>Annie<br></div></blockquote></div>"
